    "durationMs": 298661,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. The URL shortener is ready for `sh start.sh`.\n\n**What was built:**\n- `main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL` from env, connects via pgx, applies migrations, serves chi on `0.0.0.0:8000` with graceful shutdown\n- `internal/store/` — pgx-backed persistence: create (race-safe via `ON CONFLICT`), get, atomic single-statement click increment (`UPDATE ... clicks + 1 RETURNING url`), list ordered by creation id\n- `internal/migrations/` — embedded SQL with a `schema_migrations` ledger, applied idempotently in order inside transactions\n- `internal/api/` — chi router with all four routes, code validation (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), crypto-random 8-char generated codes with collision retry, and JSON error bodies (`422`/`409`/`404`)\n- `start.sh` — builds via vendored deps if needed, applies migrations, serves in foreground; `README.md` documents startup and endpoints\n\n**Verification results:**\n- 37/37 HTTP checks passed: auto/custom code creation, 409 duplicates, 422 for malformed JSON, missing/invalid URLs and codes, exact click counting, 302 Location headers, ascending list order, empty-list `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0}`\n- Restart test passed: links and click counts survive server restarts (Postgres-backed)\n- `start.sh` rebuild path verified with the binary deleted, then DB reset so the test suite starts clean"
  }
